# Protocol examples for an in-process proof host. Values are supplied only by its trusted composer.
# The --private-viewer command exercises these requests and closes the host; it prints no credentials.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000
@identity = PROCESS_SCOPED_SECRET
@bootstrap = SINGLE_EXCHANGE_SECRET
@scanId = EXACT_SCAN_ID
@sessionId = EXACT_SESSION_ID
@connectionId = EXCHANGED_CONNECTION_ID
@connectionToken = EXCHANGED_READ_SECRET

### Authenticated protocol description
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
Authorization: Bearer {{identity}}

### Exchange once; replay returns 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/viewer/exchange
Authorization: Bearer {{identity}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"ScanId":"{{scanId}}","SessionId":"{{sessionId}}","Bootstrap":"{{bootstrap}}"}

### Retained observation; stale epoch returns 400 and excluded capture returns 409
GET {{baseUrl}}/viewer/{{scanId}}/{{sessionId}}/observation?epoch=1
Authorization: Bearer {{identity}}
X-Viewer-Id: {{connectionId}}
X-Viewer-Token: {{connectionToken}}

### Revoke and acknowledge actual drain; subsequent read returns 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/viewer/{{scanId}}/{{sessionId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{identity}}
X-Viewer-Id: {{connectionId}}
X-Viewer-Token: {{connectionToken}}
